        "text": "All the specified Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] encrypt_payload.py** - Encrypts a plaintext payload with a managed key using Google Cloud KMS.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] decrypt_payload.py** - Decrypts a ciphertext payload with a managed key using Google Cloud KMS.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] envelope_encrypt.py** - Implements envelope encryption using a managed key service with Google Cloud KMS.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] sign_or_verify_key.py** - Uses a managed key service for signing or verification where supported with Google Cloud KMS.\n5. **[HELPER] security_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Key Management and Encryption with Google Cloud KMS.\n6. **[HELPER] security_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Key Management and Encryption with Google Cloud KMS.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] key_usage_summary.py** - Placeholder for summarizing key usage and crypto events.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] payload_safety.py** - Placeholder for checking decrypted text payloads for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] crypto_audit_embedding.py** - Placeholder for embedding crypto audit notes for semantic search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] compliance_note_translate.py** - Placeholder for translating encryption or compliance notes for reviewers.\n\nEach scored implementation file integrates with Google Cloud services and includes provider-specific identifiers as required.",
